{
  "version": 8,
  "name": "Renters paying 30%+ of income",
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Share of renter households spending 30% or more of income on gross rent \u2014 the federal definition of rent-burdened \u2014 pale mauve to deep magenta. Measured over all 83,901 tracts with a published value: 7 classes with breaks at 25%/35%/45%/55%/70%/85%, which fall at the 11th/23rd/41st/62nd/87th/97th percentile of the national distribution. 38.06% of tracts have a coefficient of variation above 0.3 at this geography, too many to fade without washing the map out, so read pct_rent_burdened_moe in the GeoParquet before drawing a conclusion from any single tract.",
    "portolan:column": "pct_rent_burdened",
    "portolan:breaks": [
      25,
      35,
      45,
      55,
      70,
      85
    ]
  },
